                  text: "Explain how serious nervous system disorders impact quality of life.",
                  exemplar: "Managing Talk for Learning: With the aid of pictures and videos, learners discuss conditions, diseases, and injuries that can cause nervous system problems (cerebral palsy, multiple sclerosis, stroke, vascular disorders, injuries, especially injuries to the head and spinal cord, etc.).\n\nProject-Based Learning: Learners work in groups, referring to appropriate literature and engaging in community interactions (experiences) to enumerate diseases and injuries that can cause structural, biochemical, or electrical abnormalities in the brain, spinal cord, or other nerves and the resulting symptoms (paralysis, muscle weakness, poor coordination, loss of sensation, seizures, confusion, pain, altered levels of consciousness, etc.).",
